<title>BELGIUM: EU says clears Daimler-Benz/Leica deal.</title>
<headline>EU says clears Daimler-Benz/Leica deal.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Commissin said on Tuesday it had cleared the acquisition by Temic Telefunken Microelectronic GmbH, a unit of Daimler-Benz, and Switzerland's Leica AG of ADC Automotive Distance Control Systems GmbH.  </p>
<p>ADC is a new company that will develop, manufacture and market cruise control systems based on infrared or radar technology, used for automatic control of road speed.</p>
<p>The Commission said in a statement that the parent companies would face competition from other international companies such as Bosch, Siemens AG and Philips Electronics NV, which are also preparing to enter Europe's distance speed-control market, valued at 20 million Ecus.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
